Hello to you all,

first thing first; we should try to define our terms. These are my 
definitions:

Cheat: Going outside of the game to try to do what ever one wants to 
doby using mechanisms like: copying save files, creating wizmode bones, 
patching and compiling and changing the existing game mechanism etc.

Abuse: Using exsiting bug that has been reported to try to circumvent 
what the devteam has tried to mean how the game should be played.

Conduct: Not using a game mechanism that has been coded in the game by 
the devteam.

So for example using 'Elbereth' is not a cheat, nor is reading blessed 
scroll of remove curse while confused, nor is naming individual objects 
of stackable objects (how could you create Sting if this wasn't 
possible; or do you mean that naming Sting is a cheat or an abuse?).

All restrictions you make for your own play are conducts; not necessary 
official ones but condacts all the same.

If you think that a game mechanism makes the game too easy, you can 
always try to convince devteam to accept your patch. But remember: the 
game is already one of the hardest computer games exiting.

Topi

